## Sylloo App Base

- `rishadblack/sylloo-app-base` is the shared base of the Sylloo apps (Sylloo POS, the Sylloo App desktop and Android): office calls of a device, sign in with browser (member or employee), PIN and idle lock, device states, activation, the release frame, updates, the REST client with the waiting list and saved data, and the shared screens. It holds no business logic: the app adds its own work. Activate the `sylloo-app-base-development` skill whenever you change device, sign-in, PIN, state, REST or screen code in an app built on it.
- The app binds its storage in a service provider: `Contracts\DeviceStore`, `Contracts\MemberDirectory` and `Contracts\ReleaseSteps` (one business) or `Contracts\DeviceEntries` (several); optionally `Contracts\BrowserOpener`, `Contracts\AppUpdater`, `Contracts\Notifier`. Screens reach the current activation only through `app(DeviceEntries::class)->current()`.
- Call the office with `Erp\OfficeClient::for($entry->state, $token)` and read `Erp\OfficeAnswer` (`ok()`, `isPending()`, `isRefused()` + `refusal()` as `Erp\RefusalCode`, `isUnreachable()`, `text()`); never read a raw Response or catch a connection error in a screen.
- The REST door (`rest/v1` on the business host): `Rest\RestClient::forDevice($state, $token)` (the activation's `business.rest_url`; `RestClient::for($host, …)` for a host the app names) `->list('leave-requests', $since)` / `->read('home')` / `->run('attendance/punch', $fields)` / `->upload($path)` read as `Rest\RestResult` (`serverTime()`, `anchor()`). Every write carries an `Idempotency-Key` header (made for you); read `code`, never `message`. The wire format lives only in `Rest\RestWire`. Offline writes go to `Rest\WaitingList` (allowed actions only: config `sylloo-app-base.rest.waiting.actions` or `WaitingList::allow()`; files as `add($action, $fields, files: ['selfie' => $path])`, uploaded first and sent as `selfie_file_id`), sent in order with `send($client)`; refused writes are kept with their reason. Lists kept on the device: `Rest\SavedData`.
- The shared screens are plain logic classes (`Screens\ActivateScreen`, `SignInScreen`, `CreatePinScreen`, `PinScreen`, `LockScreen`, `StateScreen`, `BusinessesScreen`, `PinSettingsScreen`, `AboutScreen`, `LanguageScreen`) with Livewire web faces under `/device/…` (route names `sylloo.*`). Never copy a screen into the app: add a piece at a hook place (`app(Screens\Hooks::class)->add('state.plan_ended', 'app::hooks.x')`), ask a question at a moment (`->ask('activate', 'key', fn (array $context) => new Screens\Question(…))`), register a state (`app(Device\StateRegistry::class)->register(new Device\StateDefinition(…), fn (DeviceState $d) => …)`), or listen to an event (`Events\DeviceActivated`, `PersonSignedIn`, `DeviceLocked`, `SignInEnded`, `DeviceReleased`, `PinSaved`).
- Put the `sylloo.device` middleware on the app's own pages: it sends the person to Activate, the state screen, Sign in or the lock when the device is not ready, and keeps the idle time.
- An app with its own look sets config, never copies a view: `screens.layout`, `screens.classes`, `screens.questions` (`inline` / `alert`), `icons.set` (`bootstrap` / `tabler`) + `icons.map`, `routes.screens.<screen>` (path, name, or false), `app.device_word` (`device` / `terminal` / `phone`); counted lines at a place with `Hooks::lines('state.releasing', fn (array $c) => [['text' => …, 'count' => 3]])`; its own idle lock by binding `Contracts\LockSource` (e.g. `Pin\SessionKeyLockSource`).
- An app with its own flow uses the behaviour hooks, never a copy of a screen: `Hooks::payload('activate', …)`, `check('activate.answer', …)`, `step('activate.before_keep' | 'activate.after_keep' | 'state.check' | 'sign_in.link', …)`, `refused(…)`, `sentences('<state>', …)`, `finish('signed_in', fn ($member, $offline, $person, $context) => '/terminal')`; its own notices with config `screens.notices` = `events` (`notify` / `confirm-dialog`) or its own `Contracts\ScreenNotices`. List: `docs/screens.md`.
- Texts are `Support\Texts::get('<key>')` (fills `:app` and the device word) of `sylloo-app-base::device.*` in English, Bangla and Finnish; say the device as `:device` / `:Device` / `:devices`, never a fixed word; add every new key to all three files. An app changes a text in `lang/vendor/sylloo-app-base/<locale>/device.php`. Draw with wire-bootstrap tags (`<x-wire-bootstrap::…>`); the PIN pad and the grouped code field are wire-bootstrap's `<x-wire-bootstrap::pin-pad>` / `<x-wire-bootstrap::input.code>` (the app loads wire-bootstrap's browser layer). Behaviour is Alpine components registered on `alpine:init`; no inline scripts.
- Test with `Testing\PretendOffice::start()` (answers like the API collection: `refuse()`, `pending()`, `down()`, `asMember()`, `rest()`, `assertCalled()`), `Testing\TestDevice::bind()` (`addMember()`, `enter()`), `Testing\RecordingBrowser::bind()` and `Sleep::fake()`; test a screen with `Livewire::test(Livewire\SignIn::class)->call('run', 'browser')`.
